<div class="ml-[58.9vh] p-20 text-center max-w-full">
<h1>shipping!</h1>

    <div class="bg-[#fb4bb0] rounded-xl p-5 mt-10">
    <h2>Contents</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="#What">What is shipping? & Readme requirements</a></li>
        <li><a href="#Publishing">Publishing your game</a></li>
    </ul>
    </div>

<div class="bg-[#fb4bb0] rounded-xl p-5 mt-10" id="What">
    <h2>What is shipping? & Readme requirements</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">Shipping is when you publicise your project and submit it for review. This means you'll need a good readme - at a minimum, you should include what your project is, some screenshots, how to install it, and give credits to any resources you used! heres an <a href="https://github.com/variidian/kolourmeans">example</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="bg-[#fb4bb0] rounded-xl p-5 mt-10" id="Publishing">
    <h2>Publishing your game</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">Publish your game online on <a href="https://itch.io/">itch.io</a> by logging in / signing up and clicking on the arrow in the top right corner and clicking upload new project - as shown below.</p>
    <img class="mt-4" src="../../itch_screenshot1.png"> 
    <p class="mt-4">Fill in all the fields to match your game. If your game is a web export, then make sure that your 'kind of project' is set as HTML. Make sure the pricing is set as 'No Payments' as well, and that once you save the project as a 'draft' you update it to be 'public'. Once created, you should also customize your game's page by clicking the 'edit page' button. </p>
    <img class="mt-4"
</div>

<div class="bg-[#fb4bb0] rounded-xl p-5 mt-10">
<h2>Publishing your trailer</h2>
<p>Publish your trailer by uploading the video of it as a video on YouTube - you might also want to attach it onto your itch.io game page.</p>
</div>


<div class="bg-[#fb4bb0] rounded-xl p-5 mt-10">
<p>more coming soon</p>
</div>


</div>
